course: dictionary
lesson: 6283
title: Names with a story
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A capital letter at the start of a word is a clue. Montezuma starts with a capital letter, so it is the name of a person, not an ordinary word like monkey. Names can carry a story, so read the sentence around them to find out more.
explain: Montezuma, also called Moctezuma, was a famous ruler of the Aztecs in Mexico long ago, when Spanish soldiers arrived. History lessons use clue words like Aztecs, Tenochtitlan and conquest to show you that the name belongs to the past.
explain: In everyday talk, «Montezuma's revenge» is a joking name for an upset tummy. The sentence says it is caught while travelling, especially in Mexico. Always check the context: is the sentence about history, or about a joke on holiday?
fact: A proper noun is the name of a particular person, place or thing, and it starts with a capital letter.
fact: «Montezuma» (also Moctezuma) was a famous ruler, or emperor, of the Aztecs in Mexico long ago.
fact: «Montezuma's revenge» is a joking, slang name for an upset tummy caught while travelling abroad.
fact: The name appears in history lessons about the Aztecs, but in everyday talk it is usually a joke, so check the context.
exercise: «Montezuma» starts with a capital letter. What kind of word is it? | An adjective | A verb | A common noun | *A proper noun, which is a name
exercise: In a history lesson, the clue words Aztecs and Tenochtitlan tell you the text is about whom? | A holiday in Spain | A football team | A type of food | *Montezuma, the ruler of the Aztecs
exercise: «"Montezuma's revenge" is a joking American name for diarrhoea caught while travelling, especially in Mexico.» What does the phrase mean? | A game played in Mexico | *An upset tummy caught on a trip abroad, said as a joke | A famous emperor's gift to his people | A sunny day at the beach
test: Sam says «Montezuma» is just an ordinary word, like monkey. What clue proves him wrong? | It sounds like a Spanish word | *The capital letter at the start, which marks a name | The word has more than six letters | It appears in a sentence
test: In «"Montezuma's revenge" is a joking American name for diarrhoea caught while travelling, especially in Mexico», which word tells you the phrase is about a trip abroad? | Diarrhoea | Joking | American | *Travelling
exam: Ahmed reads, «Montezuma was a ruler of the Aztecs in Mexico long ago.» What is Montezuma? | A dish from Mexico | A football club | A joke about an upset tummy | *A famous ruler, or emperor, of the Aztecs
